A||||6||Simple Fiero||My Clutch Job||||8||
Z||000000||Simple Fiero||11-21-2001||12:59 AM||||Everyone told me good luck, before I got into this, and now I know why. Clutchs have got to be the biggest pain in the ass on a fiero. I mean I am no mechanic but it hasn't been easy.<BR>Here is what has happened to me so far.<BR>I bought the clutch it was a Dynapax Kit from CT. As far as who made the clutch I don't know.<BR>First my father and I jacked the car up(DUH).<BR>Next we disconnected the shifter cables.<BR>Then my father didn't count how many bolts were connecting the engine and the tranny and he went and took apart my tranfer case and I lost some tranny fluid, which you find out later is okay.<BR>I figured out he is a dumbass and smacked him in the back of the head, after I found the 6 engine to tranny bolts.<BR>We then went ahead and hoisted the engine up, and took the Tranny mounts off. I removed the engine to tranny bolts all SIX of them.<BR>Then like a bunch of idiots we stared at the car for 1/2 an hr trying to figure out why we couldn't get the tranny to separate from the engine. We are so brillant!<BR>You have to move the axles, so my father decided that we should disconnect the lower joints I said sure. He took on look at after the boot was off and decide we should call our mechanic friend. <BR>END DAY 1<P>Tuesday Evening.<BR>Mechanic Friend I think I will call him Bush Man, cause he is freaky looking. So Bush Man came over on monday to look at where we were at and called us stupid.<BR>He made us disconnect the lower sway bars(don't know if I have this right, but I think that is what they are called.).<BR>And then the axels slid right out, and I didn't have to mess with joints. All my tranny fluid is gone now.<BR>Finally after fighting and manuvering we got the tranny off and I got to see my first pressure plate. (Very Exciting for me)<BR>Took off pressure plate, by this time Bush Man was doing this on his own cause he is brilliant and we are dumb and he basically got frustated with us.<BR>Now I get to see my first clutch also very exciting, except for the fact that there was just the frame of a clutch, and no padding. It was worn down to the rivets,(heck even the rivets were smooth and almost gone) stupid previous ower, burned it to nothing.<BR>So suggested we take the fly wheel out, so that was done and now I have to get it turned cause it has tiny stress cracks and is no longer even, heat happens what can I say.<BR>So now I am 12 hrs into this with 4 hrs more to go that is if it goes smoothly.<BR>What have I leanrt from this, well basically my father is a jack ass. He wanted to put basic high stress gear oil into my tranny, and I told him that it is my car and I am getting the correct syncro mesh stuff from GM/Pontitac. He also told me I was dumb for getting my flywheel machined, I asked him if he wanted to spend another 16 hrs doing this again, He said no, and I won that one.<P>If I am missing anything ppl should know then tell me.Thanks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Craig<BR>White 88 4cyl 5speed<p>[This message has been edited by Simple Fiero (edited 11-21-2001).]||||reg||8
Z||000001||Simple Fiero||11-21-2001||01:00 AM||||Sorry ddbl post <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Simple Fiero (edited 11-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Elenor84||11-21-2001||01:24 AM||||Man o man...sounds like a ton of work...good thing I didn't do mine...considered it for over a month but then decided it was way to cold and I didn't have the time....I gave it to my machanic and got her back in a few days...nice work though...so how does it feel with the new clutch?  mine was a 84-86 transmition swap and I did the clutch while we swapped.  My friction point is alot higher up now...did u notice that difference to?<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||11-21-2001||09:36 AM||||Sounds like a typical first time Fiero clutch job to me.  A manual, etc. might have helped with what to take apart first, but it seems like you figured it out ok.  Also, you have to drain the tranny anyway - cuz the axles have to come out and it'll dump the fluid out the axle openings if you don't.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Simple Fiero||11-21-2001||10:35 AM||||That is the funny thing Ele84 I havn't got it in yet but I will report on how it feels hopefully tonight.<BR>And unfortunatly all the fluid did go out the axel openings.<BR>One plus from all this is that I got to see it all done, which is awesome.<P>Craig||||reg||6
Z||000005||Simple Fiero||11-22-2001||12:05 PM||||Okay it all done and I have switch to what ever was in my tranny to syncromesh and it gets better ever time I drive it. By tonight it should be great.<BR>Sorry Ele84 I dont' quite know what a friction point is, but if it is where the clutch starts to grab, then no mine is really low like the pedal is less then an inch away from the floor boards before it grabs.<BR>The only problem i am having is that it is stalling a lot, but that is my fault and I am practicing to correct it. <BR>All in all this clutch job was hard, but I liked it, cause it was a blast to learn what not to do next time. I could probably do it in a day now, cause I know what not to do.<P>Craig||||reg||1
Z||000006||StuGood||11-22-2001||04:44 PM||||I think the "low friction point" after a clutch replacement is what you'd expect - it's a <B>good</B> thing.  That's the way mine acted - the "clutch starts to grab" point was maybe an inch off the floor.  Also, I notice that the pedal force required seems a lot less - almost no effort to floor the clutch pedal & disengage the clutch.  Feels like the car did when it was new  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">!<P>Anyway, congratulations, and I admire your perserverance!  Every "new" job (for me) takes probably 3 to 5 times as long as it should.  The next time it's always easier. Many happy miles  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">!      ||||reg||10
